<main class="fb-container fb-main">
  <div class="fb-content">
    <h1 class="fb-title fb-title--small">Terms of Service</h1>

    <div class="fb-notice">
      <p><strong>Draft, pending legal review.</strong></p>
      <p>This page describes how FieldBrik actually works and what it expects of members. It is not yet a final legal agreement: the wording still needs review before the site takes real registrations or payments. Last edited 2 November 2026.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="fb-prose">
      <h2>1. What FieldBrik is</h2>
      <p>FieldBrik is an online building and gaming community. Members create an account, build places, publish them, play each other's places, and talk to each other in the forum and by private message. The website and the client application are both part of the service.</p>

      <h2>2. Your account</h2>
      <p>You need an account to build, publish, post or message. You are responsible for what happens on your account, so keep your password to yourself. One account per person. Accounts are not transferable and cannot be sold.</p>
      <p>If you are under the age of majority where you live, a parent or guardian must agree to these terms on your behalf. The <a href="/parents">Parents</a> section explains what an account involves in plain language.</p>

      <h2>3. Conduct</h2>
      <p>FieldBrik is a place for building and playing. The following are not allowed:</p>
      <ul class="fb-list">
        <li>Harassment, threats, hateful content, or targeting another member.</li>
        <li>Sexual content, or content that is inappropriate for a site used by children.</li>
        <li>Sharing another person's private information.</li>
        <li>Impersonating staff, or claiming a role you do not have.</li>
        <li>Exploiting bugs, automating access, or attempting to bypass moderation, permissions or the economy.</li>
        <li>Advertising, scams, or links to content that breaks these rules.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Your content</h2>
      <p>You keep ownership of the places, items and posts you create. By publishing them you give FieldBrik permission to store them, display them, and let other members visit, play and view them. You can remove your content, and removal stops it being served.</p>
      <p>Do not upload work that belongs to somebody else without permission.</p>

      <h2>5. Moderation</h2>
      <p>Staff may review content, remove it, warn an account, or restrict an account. Restrictions are recorded against the account and apply across the whole site: a restricted account cannot get around them by visiting a different page. Where a restriction has an end date, it stops applying at that time and remains in the account's history.</p>

      <h2>6. Bucks, Tickets and memberships</h2>
      <p>Tickets are earned in the service. Bucks are a premium currency. Catalog items may be sold for Tickets, for Bucks, or both. Carpenters Club is an optional paid membership; its tiers and prices are listed on the <a href="/carpenters-club">Carpenters Club</a> page.</p>
      <p>No purchase is live yet: there is no checkout on this site. Currency and membership terms, including refunds, will be published here before anything can be bought.</p>

      <h2>7. Ending an account</h2>
      <p>You may request deletion of your account at any time. FieldBrik may suspend or close an account that breaks these terms. Records of moderation actions are kept after an account closes so that restrictions cannot be evaded by making a new one.</p>

      <h2>8. Changes</h2>
      <p>These terms will change as the service is built. Material changes will be announced on the <a href="/news">News</a> page.</p>

      <h2>9. Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about these terms go to the <a href="/support">support page</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</main>

